  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 741 PM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nWe will begin to transition patterns in the long term period as upper\nridging expands over the Plains and eventually into the Southeastern\nregion. This will bring warming temperatures and an increase in\nhumidity toward the mid-late week timeframe. In fact, highs on\nWednesday will reach into the upper 80s to lower 90s with dewpoints\nclimbing into the 60s. Thankfully we will be spared from a more\nintense heat wave this time with temps in the lower 90s and dewpoints\nnear or below 70 degrees. With that said, afternoon heat indices will\nstill reach the low to mid 90s during the Wed-Fri timeframe and could\npose a risk for heat related illness for those especially sensitive\nto heat. \n\nThe forecast, especially as we head into the weekend, becomes a \nlot less uncertain as we will remain in a warm, tropical airmass \nahead of an approaching upper wave. There are still fairly \nsignificant spatial and temporal differences amongst longer range \nmodels regarding the speed of an incoming cold front that is \nprogged to impact the TN Valley next weekend. With this in mind, \nwe will stick with blended guidance and message increasing chances\n(30-65%) for showers and thunderstorms next weekend. Be sure to \ncheck back for updates throughout the week especially if preparing\nfor outdoor plans!",
